opic:editor","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2025-07-10T15:49:03Z","updated_at":"2025-07-10T17:40:05Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.4.2-stable, 4.5-beta3\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 6700S (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 32.0.21001.9024) - AMD Ryzen 9 6900HS with Radeon Graphics (16 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nI'm building an editor plugin, and I am adding to the editor's scene tree with internal nodes to hide from the user.\nSaving the .tscn file saves the internal nodes as regular nodes.\n\nChecking the .tscn file in a txt editor, there is no parameter/token to differentiate an internal node from a regular node.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open the attached project.\n2. Check the bool in the inspector to add an internal node.\n3. Save and reload the project.\n\nInternal nodes get turned into regular nodes.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[minimal-reproduction-project.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21166366/minimal-reproduction-project.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108483/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108483/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}